# The rule file of the functionality self-audit: where the fact step looks, its caps and its exclusions.
# One "key value" per line. A key that takes one value may be given once; the others add up.

# The document of the command line: its commands, options and exit codes are compared with the code, and its
# sections are what the AI judges.
cli_doc docs/cli.md
# The "##" section whose "###" sections are the commands, and the one with the table of exit codes.
commands_heading Commands
exit_codes_heading Exit codes
# The class whose "static final int NAME = N;" constants are the exit codes.
exit_codes_class ExitCodes

# Besides cli_doc, the documents whose "`type` block" mentions are compared with the registered block types.
block_doc docs/workflow-format.md

# At most this many sections are judged, one AI call each; the rest is reported as NOT MEASURED.
max_sections 40
# A section longer than this many characters is judged in parts, cut at empty lines.
max_section_chars 12000
# The version of the question a verdict answers. It is part of the digest of every section, so raising it makes every
# section be judged again: raise it when the instructions or the prompt of the workflow change what is asked.
verdict_version 1

# Options of other programs that a command's section names. Each needs its reason. With a second word, the option
# is the other program's only in a line that holds that word before it; anywhere else it is still a finding.
# resume: "docker ps -aq --filter label=..." and "docker network ls -q --filter label=...", Docker's own option.
foreign_option filter
# check: "container_args": ["scan", "--from", ...] in a workflow's JSON, an argument of the package's own tool.
foreign_option from container_args
# seal: "COPY --from=" and "RUN --mount=...,from=", options of Dockerfile instructions.
foreign_option from COPY
foreign_option mount RUN
